      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Body"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Chain 37. Work in a five-treble shell repeat as given for the Lace Scarf pattern (rows of five-tr shells separated by dc) until the body reaches 170 cm. Fasten off."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ruffle edging"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "With the right side facing, rejoin yarn at one corner of a long edge. Ch 3 (counts as first tr). Work 2 tr into the same st (3 tr total). *Work 3 tr into the next st along the edge*. Repeat all along the long edge to the far corner. Fasten off. Repeat on the other long edge."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finishing"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Weave in all ends. Wet block: soak, press gently, pin the body to its dimensions, and allow the ruffle to gather naturally along each side. Leave to dry fully before unpinning."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
